      "en": "Urziceni is a city in Ialomița County, situated in the Bărăgan Plain of southeastern Romania. It is primarily an agricultural and commercial center, benefiting from its location on a major road and railway junction connecting Bucharest to the eastern part of the country. The city's development has been driven by its role as a marketplace for the fertile agricultural hinterland. While not a major tourist destination, Urziceni gained international attention when its local football team, Unirea Urziceni, had a period of remarkable success, including winning the national league and participating in the UEFA Champions League. The flat, open landscape of the Bărăgan Plain defines the city's surroundings."
